.TH NOUST 1 "2026-09-30" "Noust 3.1.5" "Noust"
.\" Generated by scripts/generate_man.py. Do not edit by hand.
.SH NAME
noust \- deploy and manage web applications on a Linux server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noust
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Noust deploys and manages web applications on the server it runs on. It
configures the web server, obtains and renews TLS certificates, writes and
supervises systemd units, manages databases and takes backups.
.PP
Noust requires root, because everything it does writes to /etc, /var and
systemd.
.PP
Noust was called WASM until 3.0.0.
.B wasm
remains an alias of
.B noust
for the whole 3.x series, with the same commands and options.
