.SS noust web enable
Run the panel as a systemd service that survives reboots.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-host
Interface to bind to. Anything but loopback needs TLS (\-\-tls\-cert/\-\-tls\-key or \-\-self\-signed) or \-\-insecure\-http. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port
Port to listen on. Default: 8080.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-https
Serve TLS from the panel and refuse cleartext. Needs \-\-tls\-cert and \-\-tls\-key, or \-\-self\-signed.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-cert
Certificate chain to serve.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-key
Private key for the certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-signed
Serve TLS with a self\-signed certificate, minted under /etc/noust/panel\-tls and reused while it is valid.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure\-http
Serve cleartext HTTP beyond loopback. The access token and the session cookie cross the network unencrypted.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-ip
Only answer this address or network. Repeat to allow several. Restricts who connects; encrypts nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-trusted\-proxy
Believe forwarding headers from this peer. Declare the proxy that terminates TLS so the session cookie is issued with Secure.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show the detail of each step.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Rehearse without changing anything. Read\-only checks still run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never emit colour.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

